        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "aee9d1c7f559db04b1ec829bd97a016e861c01b5",
            "parents": [
                "0662e607425838f3321aa13e25c718813fddec97"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/58/84258/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Yolkee Huang",
                "email": "cweihuang@google.com",
                "username": "soimportant"
            },
            "createdOn": 1759767229,
            "author": {
                "name": "Yolkee Huang",
                "email": "cweihuang@google.com",
                "username": "soimportant"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "For the device that this targeted, isn't this always the scale?  When would we need a different scale?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yolkee Huang",
                        "email": "cweihuang@google.com",
                        "username": "soimportant"
                    },
                    "message": "In our use case, we need to read the temperature from a MCU on GPU. When using `i2cget` to get value manually, it is a 8 bit integer. We need to keep it on this value instead of divided by 1000, so that's why `scaleValue` is included."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "So this is adding a new MCU type?  I suspect we need to add a new type here:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/dbus-sensors/blob/0662e607425838f3321aa13e25c718813fddec97/src/mcu/MCUTempSensor.cpp#L58\n\nThat would then define the scaling and values present on that device."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yolkee Huang",
                        "email": "cweihuang@google.com",
                        "username": "soimportant"
                    },
                    "message": "> So this is adding a new MCU type?\n\nI don't think so. I thought that this service is designed for reading the general MCU device that exposed on i2c bus. Adding the `scaleValue` is just for increasing its flexibility.\n\nDo you mean that we should provide the default scale value for each MCU type?"
                }
            ],
